<script server>
// Enumerate this route's ids at build time. Two lines on purpose: stx's SSG
// extracts this body by regex and stops at the first line starting with `}`,
// and evaluates it via `new Function`, so there is no module scope to import
// into. Absolute path because a relative specifier has no meaningful base
// inside that evaluation context. See app/Helpers/staticPaths.ts.
export async function getStaticPaths() {
  const mod = await import(`${process.cwd()}/app/Helpers/staticPaths.ts`)
  return await mod.judgePaths()
}
</script>

{{--
  The canonical judge page — the URL in the sitemap, and the one entitySeo
  writes each judge's real title, description and Person node onto.

  It used to render a hand-written copy of the tab bar plus a summary card
  whose contents were hardcoded: "4.8/5.0", "Active", "Superior Court of
  California", "Appointed 2020", "Criminal Law, Family Law" — the same five
  values on all 2740 pages, for judges those values had nothing to do with.
  A crawler, which runs no JS and never saw the redirect below, read that as
  this judge's record. On a site whose whole subject is what is actually true
  about a judge, that is the worst possible thing to ship, and it was being
  shipped on every canonical page.

  It also ended in `@slot('content')`, which nothing filled on this route —
  the tab views fill it — so Bench/Judge/ProfileHeader bounced bare
  /judges/:id to /judges/:id/profile on mount just to get something rendered.
  That is the complaint in #64: the canonical URL advertised in the sitemap
  was a client-side redirect to a shared shell page.

  So this now renders the judge itself, from the same three components the
  profile tab uses. Mirrors /court-houses/:id, which was fixed the same way in
  37f98846 for the same reason.

  No <script client> here on purpose: the three includes carry their own
  scopes, and a block that only called useHead would both register an empty
  scope and overwrite the per-judge head that entitySeo injects at build time.
--}}

@extends('layouts/default')
@section('title', 'Judge Profile - Bench Review')
@section('content')
  {{-- No <main> here: stx-standards 2.8/3.5 put it in the layout, and
       resources/layouts/default.stx already opens one. Two landmarks per page
       is invalid HTML and announces twice to a screen reader.

       It also matters to stx itself: the runtime resolves a <script> block's
       root with `document.querySelector('main')` when it cannot find one from
       the script's siblings, and that returns the FIRST <main>. With two, a
       block taking that path binds its scope to the wrong element. --}}
  @include('Bench/Judge/ProfileHeader')
  @include('Bench/Judge/JudgeTabs')
  <div class="mx-auto px-4 py-8 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 max-w-7xl">
    @include('Bench/Judge/Profile')
  </div>
@endsection
